cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the NORMA Semantic Toolkit in your research, please cite the toolkit. If you use the NORMA-O ontology specifically, also cite it using the DOI below."
type: software
title: "NORMA Semantic Toolkit"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-23"
authors:
  - family-names: "Leyva-Sánchez"
    given-names: "Sheyla"
    affiliation: "Ontology Engineering Group, Universidad Politécnica de Madrid"
license: "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sheyls/norma-semantic-toolkit"
url: "https://w3id.org/def/norma-o"
abstract: "NORMA is an open semantic toolkit for the formal representation and computational processing of legal norms. It combines an OWL 2 DL ontology (NORMA-O), a structured BPMN-based annotation methodology, an automated knowledge graph construction pipeline, and a SWRL rule generation engine. The result is a queryable, reasoner-ready knowledge graph suitable for semantic publication, compliance support, and legal knowledge engineering."
keywords:
  - legal ontology
  - legal knowledge engineering
  - regulatory compliance
  - knowledge graph
  - OWL 2 DL
  - SWRL
  - BPMN
  - semantic web
  - norm annotation
  - ELI
  - PROV-O
